# - {SIGN_CONVENTION: 'dy_core/dx_core are the MEASURED position of the kernel core relative to the declared fiducial (0-based index 50,50).
#     They are NOT the shift to apply. The shift to APPLY to the kernel is the NEGATIVE: (dy_apply, dx_apply) = (-dy_core, -dx_core).
#     Use spherex_gpupipe.calib.psf_core_offsets.psf_core_shift(), which returns the already-negated apply-shift.'}
# - {key: '(detector, zone_id) = primary-header DETECTOR and the zone_id label in that cutout''s PSF_ZONES row for the plane used'}
