#     fallback was tested and rejected: leave-one-out, it is WORSE than the detector median for dy because dy alternates between adjacent
#     lattice rows, so the nearest zone is often in the opposite phase.'}
# - {zone_structure: 'dy varies mainly BETWEEN lattice rows (detector Y bands) and is nearly constant along a row; the row pattern alternates
#     rather than trending with wavelength. Corroborated by both independent peak estimators (corr ~0.96 across all zones), so it is a
#     real property of the delivered kernels, not estimator noise. dx is far flatter. This is why the table is per-zone and not a scalar.'}
# - {not_the_correction: 'dy_centroid/dx_centroid are the full-array flux centroid, stored for diagnostics only. They mix the rigid core
